  "details": "1. With secure boot disabled attempt to start vrc\n\n2. EAC will give an error showing you need to have secure boot enabled\n\n1. With windows core isolation disabled attempt to start vrc\n\n2. EAC will give an error showing you need HVCI enabled\n\nBoth of these were not the case a day or two ago and there has been no updates as far as i can see. This also only occurred on one machine. The eac version looks to be the same on both machines the only difference is the windows version. The one getting the issue is on a newer build of windows.\n\nThe secure boot is a somewhat easy fix just causes issues with wanting to use Linux.\n\nThe second is less easy to fix as the Bluetooth driver that is needed by my link box to control the base stations is not compatible with HVCI.\n\nMy headset is a vive pro 2\n\nDXdiag available upon request",
